meta {
  name: Update Asset Subpath
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

patch {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/assets/6aa021b72b6fd055ffb7ca9f/alt_text
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  "WC test via subpath"
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.alt_text: eq WC test via subpath
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08. `PATCH /assets/{id}/{path}` has zero spec
  detail (matches Phase 0's pattern for every subpath route), but works
  the same way the `GET` subpath does: `{path}` names a single field
  (here `alt_text`), and the request body is that field's raw new value
  (a bare JSON string, not wrapped in an object) -- not a partial-object
  PATCH like the root `PATCH /assets/{id}` uses. Response is the **full**
  updated asset object, same shape as the root PATCH.
}
